A Python CLI/library generated from the Artemis `py-tool` template. Managed with
[uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/).

## Develop

```bash
uv sync              # create .venv and install dev dependencies from the lockfile
uv run {{ project_name }}   # run the console script
```

## Gates (run before pushing; CI runs them too)

```bash
uv run ruff check .        # lint
uv run ruff format --check .  # format
uv run pyright             # typecheck (strict)
uv run pytest --cov        # test with coverage (floor in [tool.coverage.report])
uv run python scripts/mutation.py  # would a test notice if the code were wrong?
```

CI runs the shared Artemis pipelines (`ci`, `security`{% if visibility == 'public' %}, `codeql`{% endif %}) on every PR via
[ci-python.yml](https://github.com/willzhu16/platform). Behaviour is customised through
tool config in `pyproject.toml` (ruff, pyright, pytest), never by renaming commands.

`scripts/mutation.py` is the one worth understanding. Coverage proves a line ran; the
mutation score proves a test would have objected. It rewrites `src/` many ways and fails if
too few of those edits break a test. Note that pytest `addopts` is deliberately free of
`--cov`: coverage collection fights mutmut's tracer, so the coverage floor lives in
`[tool.coverage.report]` and CI passes `--cov` on the command line. Do not move it back.

**Write acceptance criteria with ids.** In the task packet, number each one
(`- AC-1: an expired token is rejected`), and claim it from a test by putting `AC-1:` in the
test name. A criterion you can only check by hand gets no id — say in the PR how you
checked it. Never lower a floor to turn a red build green; add the missing test. The full
standard is the
[testing standard](https://github.com/willzhu16/platform/blob/v1/handbook/testing-standard.md).
